  "description": "Sustainable Development Goals is a dataset listed in energydata.info, an open data portal for energy in developing countries under the section \"Agriculture\", published or maintained by World Bank Group. Relevant indicators drawn from the World Development Indicators, reorganized according to the goals and targets of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). These indicators may help to monitor SDGs, but they are not always the official indicators for SDG monitoring. Coverage: 182 countries. It has 8 files in XLS, DATABANK, API. The portal files it under Agriculture. The portal gives 2022 as the release date. It is reached through the links recorded on this page, with the catalogue entry as the discovery route. Access is free of charge and open. The licence is CC-BY-4.0. Caveats: this record was written from the catalogue listing only, so the linked page was not opened, its contents and current availability were not checked, and the description may lag the source. Suitability for infrastructure simulation has not been checked. Related record: the catalogue-level record data-energydata-info-world-bank.",
